---
capability: returns/submit-a-return
---
# Submit a return

- A customer sends back items only from an order that has been delivered {#delivered-only}
  e.g. an order that is paid but not yet delivered -> the return is refused with "Only delivered orders can be returned"
- A customer sends items back within thirty days of the moment of delivery {#return-window}
  e.g. delivered on 1 January -> a return on 31 January is accepted, one on 5 February is refused
- A customer sends back only products that are on the order {#product-on-order}
  e.g. an order of wool socks, a return naming a headlamp -> refused with "Product headlamp is not on order"
- A customer sends back no more of a product than the order holds {#quantity-within-order}
  e.g. one pair of wool socks ordered, two sent back -> refused with "Cannot return more wool-socks than were ordered"
- A quantity sent back is a whole number of at least one {#whole-quantity}
  e.g. half a rain jacket -> refused with "Quantity must be a whole number of at least 1"
- A return names at least one item {#at-least-one-item}
  e.g. a return submitted with an empty list of items -> refused with "A return needs at least one item"

